course: dictionary
lesson: 11938
title: Speaking with candour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Candour means being honest and open, and saying what you really think. Often the truth is not nice to hear, but a person with candour says it anyway. «The coach spoke with candour: "We lost because we did not train hard."»
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. In «Her candour surprised the class», the word surprised tells you that she said something the class did not expect. Ask yourself: is the person hiding something, or telling it straight? If they tell it straight, that is candour.
explain: Candour is not the same as being rude. A friend who is open about your mistakes wants to help you get better. Their honesty is kind in its purpose, even when the words sting a little.
fact: Candour means honesty and openness.
fact: Candour is a noun, and you cannot count it: you say «some candour», not «a candour».
fact: Candour often means saying something true that is not nice to hear.
fact: «Her candour surprised the class» means she spoke honestly and openly, and people did not expect it.
fact: A good friend may show candour about your mistakes, to help you improve.
exercise: «She spoke with candour about the broken vase.» What does candour mean here? | Hiding the truth to keep everyone happy | Shouting very loudly | Saying nothing at all | *Being honest and open about what really happened
exercise: «Her candour surprised the class.» Which word is closest in meaning to candour? | Fear | *Honesty | Anger | Silence
exercise: A good friend tells you, with candour, that your plan has a flaw. What does the friend show? | Rudeness, just to hurt you | Pretend praise to avoid upsetting you | *Openness and honesty, even when the news is hard | Secrecy and hiding things
test: «The mayor answered the reporters with candour about the money that had gone missing.» What does candour mean here? | Telling jokes to change the subject | *Speaking honestly and openly, even about bad news | Whispering so nobody can hear | Refusing to answer any questions
test: Which sentence shows candour? | «Everything is fine, nothing happened here.» | «I have no idea who did it.» | *«I broke the window, and I will pay to fix it.»
exam: What does candour mean? | Keeping secrets from your family | Being very quick at running | *Being honest and open, saying what you truly think | Hiding your feelings
